---
source: apps/oxcruise/tests/cli.rs
expression: table.stdout
---
correctness (default: error)
  no-circular                Reports dependencies that are part of a circular chain of imports and shows the shortest cycle through each of them.
  no-cross-package-relative  Reports relative imports (`../other-package/src/x`) that reach into another workspace package.
  no-dev-deps-in-prod        Reports production modules importing packages that are only in `devDependencies`.
  no-test-imports            Reports non-test modules importing test files (`*.test.*`, `*.spec.*`) or test directories (`test`, `tests`, `__tests__`, `__mocks__`).
  no-undeclared-deps         Reports imports of installed npm packages that no `package.json` section declares.
  no-unresolvable            Reports imports that could not be resolved to a file or package.

suspicious (default: warn)
  no-deprecated              Reports imports of Node.js built-in modules that Node has deprecated, such as `sys` or `punycode`, and of npm packages whose `package.json` marks them as deprecated.
  no-duplicate-deps          Reports packages declared in more than one `package.json` section, for example both `dependencies` and `devDependencies`.
  no-orphans                 Reports modules that no other module imports and that import nothing.

style (default: off)

restriction (default: off)
  internal-modules           Go-style `internal` directories: code under `a/b/internal/` may only be imported from code under `a/b/`.
  layers                     Enforces a layered architecture: each layer may import only the layers it lists in `allow`.
  no-optional-deps           Reports use of optional dependencies, which may not be installed.
  no-peer-deps               Reports use of peer dependencies, which the consuming project must provide.

nursery (default: off)

13 rules
